{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GxpeMsxa7pyGi2jUJ7NVc2","type":"tool_result","content":"30\t\tPathEnv    string   // PATH for host jobs; default the controller's PATH\n31\t\tAllowEnv   []string // model-key names; default ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN\n32\t\tAllowFixed []string // names allowed in Command.Fixed; default CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, DISABLE_AUTOUPDATER, CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC, CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_BACKGROUND_TASKS\n33\t\t// ConfigDirEnv is the Fixed name whose value must equal View.ConfigDir,\n34\t\t// the job's own config dir. Default CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR.\n35\t\tConfigDirEnv string\n36\t\tKillGrace    time.Duration // default 10s\n37\t\tBuildTimeout time.Duration // default 15m\n38\t\tNow          func() time.Time\n39\t\tLog          *slog.Logger\n40\t\t// OnHostUntrusted, if set, is called once per host-mode job that reads\n41\t\t// untrusted input, right after the process starts. serve records an\n42\t\t// events row through it. nil = log only.\n43\t\tOnHostUntrusted func(ctx context.Context, h executor.Handle) error\n44\t\n45\t\t// Sidecar clone (see sidecar.go).\n46\t\tSidecarGit     sidecarGit               // default gitx.New(\"\")\n47\t\tSidecarURL     func(repo string) string // default https://github.com/<repo>.git\n48\t\tSidecarToken   gitx.TokenFunc           // nil = no auth header (local remotes in tests)\n49\t\tSidecarTimeout time.Duration            // init + fetch + export bound; default 2m\n50\t\n51\t\t// CloneDir, if set, is the only repository Cleanup runs git worktree\n52\t\t// admin in. A handle whose RepoDir differs (stored before #113, when\n53\t\t// RepoDir was the operator's checkout) has its worktree made writable and\n54\t\t// removed with os.RemoveAll, with no git call, and one\n55\t\t// executor.cleanup_foreign_repo Info log. \"\" = always use h.RepoDir.\n56\t\tCloneDir string\n57\t}\n58\t\n59\t// Local implements executor.Executor on this host.\n60\ttype Local